      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_514566d4",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman affectionately holding multiple pets (a golden retriever and several kittens), overlaid with text that reads: \"why do 'white people' own so many pets? because we're not allowed to own people anymore.\" This meme uses a racially charged stereotype, implying that white people own pets as a substitute for owning human beings, which is a harmful and hateful trope rooted in racist historical and social narratives. The intent is to demean and dehumanize a racial group by invoking a false and offensive historical analogy, suggesting that white people are inherently incapable of owning human beings, which is both factually incorrect and deeply offensive. The meme relies on racialized language and harmful stereotypes to provoke a reaction, making it clearly hateful and potentially harmful to its target audience.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_7c62f9f2"
      },
